WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.870
A person can become immortal by leaving

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.880
something behind for
the next generation.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.360
No, Aka-chan.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.340
Immortality is only possible by

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.470
consuming and bathing in the
blood of young maidens.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.320
Why are you talking about
Elizabeth Bathory?

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.470
It's scary!

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.100
What I'm trying to say is...

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.380
What can the student council leave
behind for the next generation?

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.930
That's our topic for today.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.000
Because... we graduate tomorrow.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:35.110
Hekiyou Academy
32nd Graduation

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.550
So that's it.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.560
Yeah. And Mafuyu and I
are transferring, too.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.930
Tomorrow is graduation...

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.000
This is our last student council meeting.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.640
What to leave our successors...

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.560
Some kind of cursed ritual?

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.670
I'm sure they'd rather we didn't.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.910
Besides, Hekiyou doesn't
have any curses.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.390
Very well.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.930
Mafuyu will leave her
hand-drawn doujinshi of

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:39.270
you and Nakameguro-senpai.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.060
I'd rather you didn't!

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.930
I'll leave them all of my
finished H-games, then.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.570
That's worth even less!

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:48.850
What?

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.570
Okay, no stupid fights.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:56.670
Like I said, the student council
should leave something behind.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.760
Okay, what do you want to leave?

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.080
I think we should leave something cute!

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.680
Like a bear!

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.190
Do you want us to make

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.950
a stuffed animal or carve
a bear out of wood?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.090
No, we should go to the mountains

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.550
and get a real one.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:13.890
That's really dangerous!

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:14.800
A baby bear.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.110
That's not the issue!

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:19.190
What will next year's student
council do with a bear?

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.960
Five members and a bear?

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.530
Fine. A tiger or a lion, instead.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.650
Why do you keep
suggesting deadly animals?

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.450
What are you expecting from
the next student council?

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.970
Fluffiness?

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:40.360
What do you think the student council
should leave behind, Chizuru-sama?

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.720
Hmm...

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.600
How about a huge sum of money to drive

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.220
everyone mad with greed?

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.590
That's not something
you say with a smile!

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:51.360
I don't think there are any normal people

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.860
on the student council this term.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.860
Talk about calling the kettle black, Key-kun.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:55.730
That's right.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.530
Anyway, let's calm down.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.150
Everybody's thinking about what

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.660
they personally want to leave behind.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.190
Well, if you ask somebody
what they want to leave,

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:08.180
it's natural for it to be something personal.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.470
You guys busy?

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.320
Something to leave for the
next student council, huh?

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.080
Well, what did you get from
the previous student council?

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.190
You could learn something from that.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.660
As usual, that's very blunt,

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.450
but strangely good advice.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.470
But we didn't get anything
from them, did we?

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.130
That's right.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.070
Leaving something for the
next student council is

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.820
an idea I came up with.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:39.490
So it's not a tradition?

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:40.650
It is.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.460
It's a tradition from now on.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:45.090
I'm a trailblazer, Sugisaki.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.780
I hope the next student council

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.950
blazes the opposite trail.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.720
How about when you were
a student, sensei?

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:58.230
Did the graduates leave
anything for the next class?

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.960
I wasn't on the student
council, so I couldn't say.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.600
I suppose they left the
seeds of future trouble?

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.630
Your graduates were horrible!

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:09.620
Did any of them leave anything useful?

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.170
If you really want some advice, then...

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:14.380
I know.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:19.510
You could give some money to me,
the advisor, for next year's lunches.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:20.380
Okay, everyone.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.430
The five of us will figure it out.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.380
Right.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.700
Make sure you don't
pass on the habit

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.620
of being rude to the advisor, okay?

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:34.570
When you think about it,

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:37.770
most of the things we'd be
leaving them are pretty serious.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.500
Like documents or manuals.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.320
Those are boring!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.510
I want to leave something more fun!

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:49.310
That brings us back to square one,
and our conflicting personal tastes.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.880
I want something fun for all,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.820
not something just one person wants.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:54.670
But still...

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.010
Why don't we look at this
from the other direction?

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:00.980
The other direction?

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.590
Yes. Why don't we think about
what the next student council

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:08.970
would want us to leave,
instead of what we want to leave them?

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.080
What the next student
council would want...

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.170
Wouldn't that be stuff
like manuals and things?

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:20.040
They'll get that whether
we do anything or not.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.310
No, not just directions and stuff...

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:26.500
Something that expresses our experiences.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.040
In other words, you want

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:32.650
to leave something written
in our own words, right?

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.700
That's right.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:35.560
Chizuru?

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.900
Don't we already have the
perfect gift, then?

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.560
As long as they have these,

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:50.310
they'll have most of what
we felt and experienced.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:55.460
This is something that
belongs to each of us,

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.130
but let's leave it behind.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:03.820
I want this to stay in the
student council room.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.200
Yeah.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:13.700
So we're leaving these for
the next student council.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.430
Good luck, Sugisaki.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.440
We're through with discussions.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.840
Our last student council
meeting is nearly over.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.100
Is it all right to let
it end like this?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.640
Without saying anything?

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.530
Okay, on to our next topic.

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:42.960
There's another topic?

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.830
There's two today?

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.860
"Leave it better than you found it"?

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.180
So then...

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:52.570
Everybody ready?

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:53.470
Yeah.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.370
Where do we start?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.930
I'm not good at the little stuff,

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.660
so I'll move the shelves and things.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.950
Mafuyu will sweep!

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:06.200
The corners of the room
are my territory!

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.750
I'll clean the windows
and the high places!

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.720
Bring me a stool!

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:11.990
Right, right.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:16.110
You can clean the low
spots with me, okay?

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:20.350
I'll take the high places, then.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.020
7:58?

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:35.100
The clock's stopped.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.910
That clock is broken.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.780
Changing the batteries didn't work.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.780
I don't want to leave
behind a broken clock.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:44.980
Let's replace it with a new one, then.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.160
We've still got some
budget money.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.490
That's a good idea.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.530
Let's restock all the supplies, too.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:55.000
There's the hole I made in the wall.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.530
I'd like to buy
something to patch it.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.490
Then Mafuyu wants to

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:02.170
add more memory to the
student council's PCs.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.120
That's right!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:05.540
It's always good to be prepared!

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.030
Let's all go shopping!

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.040
Yeah!

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:15.450
Did everybody get what they need?

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:17.850
It would be wonderful
to have a bed to relax on

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.830
in the student council room.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.460
It's not your house.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.810
This would be useful for
eliciting confessions.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:26.560
Who are you going to be torturing?

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.630
It'd be convenient to have a faucet
in the student council room.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.190
You could wash your hands
quickly, and drink water.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:34.200
Setting that up would
involve construction work.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.070
A bath would be nice, too!

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:39.710
Bathing in the student council room?

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:42.980
I think the student council should
be a little more relaxed.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:46.580
Sure, that would be nice, but I
think that's taking it too far.

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:49.330
If there's nothing else to buy,
I'm going to the register.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:50.720
Oh, hello.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:53.130
It's the man who bought
all those H-games.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.660
They let you out of jail?

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.390
O-Out of jail?

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:58.730
You haven't changed a bit, Minase.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.110
So you're out shopping
for the student council.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:02.600
Yeah.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:06.600
Was it worth all the hard
work it took to get in?

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:07.660
Of course.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:08.870
Not a second of hesitation.

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.520
It's thanks to you, Minase.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:11.240
Thanks.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.140
Shouldn't you be telling them that?

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:21.380
Goodbye, and say hello
to your jailer for me.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:22.010
No,

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:25.030
I'll be back at Hekiyou next year!

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:30.390
Shopping took more time and
energy than I thought.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.720
Okay, so...

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:32.780
You're going to treat?

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:33.660
You are.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.400
Why me?

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.780
I'll take the
Salisbury steak special,

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.360
the mixed fry,
and the katsudon!

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.700
Mafuyu will have pancakes and

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.140
a chocolate parfait and
New York cheesecake!

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.640
You're ordering all that?

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:48.930
I'll have caviar, truffle pasta,
and sautéed foie gras.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.410
They don't sell foie gras here...

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:53.970
Oh, fine.

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:56.550
We can get cake and soda.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.970
Maybe I could say it here...

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.980
I could thank them for everything.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.160
Brother!

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:08.650
Eris-chan!

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:10.160
Welcome!

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.910
This is one of the chain stores my dad runs.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:16.670
So you can order whatever you like.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:17.530
Really?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:18.750
Thanks!

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.350
Is it right to be so happy over

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:21.700
a kid giving you free food?

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:25.470
Sister!

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:26.950
Excellent timing.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.800
I was wondering what to
publish in my last paper

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.370
before the graduation ceremony.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.790
Can I have an interview
with the student council?

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.080
That sounds fun!

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.590
I want to ask you things, too!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.190
Sure, what do you want to know?

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:43.600
Have you all gotten
physical with brother?

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.200
This is a scoop!

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:49.430
Orgies at the student council!

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:50.900
XXX rated!

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:54.320
The shocking truth revealed
just before graduation!

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:55.720
Wow!

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.750
It's nothing like that!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:01.650
We just went to
do a little shopping.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.540
But now it's really late.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.440
We're back.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.530
I have to say it.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:07.550
This time...

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.460
The lights are on in the
student council room.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.250
You're right.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:13.980
Did we forget to turn them off?

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.200
Brother!

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.230
You're late. What were you doing?

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:21.740
Ringo and Asuka?

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.180
What are you doing here?

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.780
The door was unlocked.

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:26.020
You should be more careful.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.240
What are you doing here?

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.910
I heard tomorrow was graduation...

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:33.030
So Ringo wanted to say
goodbye to everyone.

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:36.900
I heard that Minatsu-san and
Mafuyu-san are transferring.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:37.650
I see.

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:42.840
I'm happy to see all
my rivals leaving.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:45.550
But you did come to say goodbye.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.370
Thank you.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:50.270
You haven't changed a bit.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:53.170
Go to hell, everyone!

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.100
Wh-What does that mean, Ringo-chan?

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.380
Well, it means I want to
spend more time with you,

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.510
so we can all go to hell and
spend eternity together!

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:07.250
Ringo-san is a powerful rival.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:12.020
It makes me sad to think
you won't be here anymore.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.960
Sugisaki will be here,
so you can come see him.

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:16.960
Yeah!

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:19.460
Well, no point in just standing here.

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:21.900
Let's go home, my love.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.610
I'm not your love!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:24.600
"Darling," then?

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:25.880
I'm not your darling, either!

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:26.670
Then "Spot."

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:28.910
"Spot"? That's a dog's name!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.670
We'll be back!

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:33.470
Bye!

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:35.150
See you again, guys.

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:36.240
Take care.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.340
Right, thank you!

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:43.470
It's been a busy day.

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:48.280
Before the day is over...

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.750
We got a new clock...

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.700
And the room's clean.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.160
We've completed this, then.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.840
Wearing a boring outfit
leads to a boring life!

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.780
There's still more?

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.580
Will this meeting never end?

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:16.220
I think we should change
into new uniforms.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:19.220
I've always wanted to wear
a sailor uniform.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.150
Even though you're graduating tomorrow?

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:25.070
I've always wanted a black cape.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.000
Are you going to be practicing black magic?

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.650
You're right, though.

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:31.640
There's no sense in discussing a
new uniform at this point.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.060
That's right.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.370
I think we should talk about things
we can only discuss today.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.860
Things we can only discuss today?

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.610
Yeah, that's right.

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:45.610
Truly important things
can't be expressed in words.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.760
How many times has she yelled
something like that today?

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:52.120
And nothing has been very helpful.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.760
I'm not just doing this for me!

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.030
I'm doing it for the world,
and for the viewers!

00:14:58.550 --> 00:14:59.970
If we took a survey that asked

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.700
"Why do you watch Student
Council's Discretion,"

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:06.030
90% of the answers would read,
"To listen to the President."

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.470
So, Aka-chan, what's our topic?

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.040
It's, um...

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.440
Souji and Touji!

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.390
Let's think about these two words.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.420
We're done cleaning <i>(souji)</i>.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:20.490
And winter solstice
<i>(touji)</i> was a while ago.

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:21.450
We ate squash and everything.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.950
Not that souji and touji!

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.490
You need to write in kanji for
people to know what you mean.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.690
The farewell address and reply, right?

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:31.490
Yeah, that's right.

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:35.260
But you're giving the reply
at graduation, aren't you?

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:37.290
Don't tell me you haven't
thought of anything.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.910
So you're using the
student council for

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.500
personal reasons again, aren't you?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:46.750
Graduation is a big deal for
everyone, so it's okay!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:50.090
Well, I suppose it does have
something to do with school.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.540
So, who's got a good reply?

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:52.920
You're just having us do it?

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:55.630
At least make an outline for us.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:56.280
An outline?

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:58.320
We don't need anything elaborate,

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:00.920
but we at least need a general idea
of what you want to say

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.670
if you want our help.

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:06.590
I want to include the words,
"Stop in the name of the shogun!"

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.660
That makes it even harder to help!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.520
This isn't a period drama.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:12.170
Okay...

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:16.110
We can make it more modern.
"An RPG that will move your heart."

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:18.310
What are you advertising
during our graduation?

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:21.040
Stop complaining and help, okay?

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.180
I know you're doing the reply,
but who's doing the farewell address?

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.450
Sugisaki.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:28.030
Me?

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:29.450
In terms of who's the better candidate,

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:32.190
it's 800,000:2 in Minatsu's favor.

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:34.140
She's that much better?

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:36.950
But Minatsu and Mafuyu-chan
are transferring, right?

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:40.550
I thought it'd be weird to
have someone leaving the

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:42.060
school give the farewell address.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.490
That's right.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:47.700
Then why don't we have Key-kun
give a farewell address,

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:51.230
and then Aka-chan can reply to it.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.570
That's a good idea.

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:55.670
Farewell Address:

00:16:56.130 --> 00:17:00.080
It is spring, and the wind
lifts up the girls' skirts.

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:03.410
The boys' crotches are waiting
for their moment to bloom...

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.960
Reply: Die.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.740
What kind of graduation
ceremony is this?

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.330
Aka-chan was pretty harsh...

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:11.230
But it's totally
your fault, senpai.

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:12.900
Forget the season stuff.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.760
Talk about something important.

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:16.230
Fine.

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:17.540
Farewell Address.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:19.330
I love you, President.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.510
Reply. I'm sorry.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.700
That's not what the graduation
ceremony is for!

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.600
I said what was important.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.380
I said what I wanted to say.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:30.710
And I gave an appropriate reply.

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.200
If you think it's so
easy, then you try it.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.390
It's hard.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:36.850
Farewell Address.

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:39.330
Even after graduation, I hope the boys

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:41.420
will continue to be good friends!

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:42.380
Reply.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:44.360
Our adventure is just beginning.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:45.680
You're doing it wrong!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:49.720
Mafuyu was just talking about
the wonders of friendship.

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:52.430
No, I'm sure there was
more to it than that!

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:56.060
I gave a very appropriate reply
to end a graduation ceremony.

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:58.570
Yours was more like the
end of a canceled manga!

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.410
Listen, you two.

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:02.720
You can't just say what you want.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:05.190
You have to represent
everyone's feelings.

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:08.020
Chizuru-san, let's do this ourselves.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:08.790
Yeah.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.200
Farewell, graduates.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.420
Farewell, underclassmen.

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:15.520
That was too short!

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:19.100
Now I have <i>no</i> idea what to do!

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:22.960
Maybe you'll just have to
figure it out by yourself, then?

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:24.730
It's not that easy!

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:26.540
What would you say, Sugisaki?

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.170
I would...

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:35.670
I would say it in my own words.

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.910
Since it's our last goodbye.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.990
People want to hear
your true feelings.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:47.750
That's what the students
here at Hekiyou are like.

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:51.630
They're the kind of people who'd
choose you to be president.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:52.980
Sugisaki.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:58.090
All right.

00:18:58.090 --> 00:18:58.840
I'll do that.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.600
This topic's been covered, then.

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:05.040
Let's go home.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:07.440
What's our next topic?

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:09.530
It's time to go home.

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:10.950
It's pitch black outside.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:12.100
That's right.

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:12.910
Yeah.

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:15.030
Wait.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.340
What's wrong, Sugisaki?

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:19.320
Sorry.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.060
But...

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.830
I can't let it end like this.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.160
Key-kun?

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:27.970
What are you talking about, Ken?

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.920
All day I've told myself
I had to say something.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.830
But I couldn't find the words.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.840
Now I have them.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:39.700
I should just be honest
about how I feel.

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:41.970
How you feel?

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:49.270
How much I love this student
council, and everyone in it.

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.060
I...

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:58.060
I'd like to hear those words.

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.530
Mafuyu, too.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.560
Me, too.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:01.370
Yeah.

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:02.930
Me, too.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:05.830
Thank you.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:09.350
I'll speak to each of
you in turn, then.

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.860
First, Mafuyu-chan.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:14.670
Okay.

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.200
I love you, Mafuyu-chan.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.230
I love you for the kindness

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:21.220
you showed when we met
in that winter park.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.760
I love the way you smile when
you're enjoying your hobbies.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.640
Don't be nervous at your new school.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:31.890
Show everyone what a unique
and strange person you are.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:33.700
Right!

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:36.220
Minatsu.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:36.980
Yeah.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:40.710
I love your warmth and your strength.

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:44.570
That noble strength
you gained to protect

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.050
what you care about.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:50.590
And your warmth, like the sun,
that makes everyone like you.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:52.880
Jeez...

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:56.030
I'm sure you'll be the center of attention

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:59.160
at your new school,
and make everybody smile.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:02.960
You'll always be someone
I can be proud of, right?

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:04.650
Yeah, of course!

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:07.610
Chizuru-san.

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:08.280
Yes.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:13.410
I love the pure heart that lies
beneath your pure exterior.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.380
Key-kun...

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:16.020
I love your calm rationality,

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:18.010
which makes you the most
reliable when things get bad.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:22.890
And finally, I admire your deep compassion.

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:27.420
And your delicate, pure heart.

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:28.780
Thank you.

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:29.970
I think you're only

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:33.680
going to become more and more
attractive from here on out.

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:35.120
But...

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:40.670
I still want you to be the girl
who messes around with us.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.580
Of course I will.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:45.690
That's who I am.

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:49.370
President.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:50.330
Yes?

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:52.730
I love you as you are.

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:54.310
As I am?

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.800
Innocence itself.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:21:59.360
A person who's always true to herself,

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:01.880
who thinks about what she did wrong

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.860
when someone gets mad at her.

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:07.950
A person who can do the most
difficult things with ease.

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:10.450
Someone who grows so much every day.

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:13.060
Somebody with the ability to
make everyone smile.

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:16.940
Watching you grow up makes me very happy.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:20.180
But no matter how much you grow,

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:24.110
I want you to stay Sakurano Kurimu,
the person you are now.

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:26.340
Of course!

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.580
I'll always be me.

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:31.730
I'm glad...

00:22:32.390 --> 00:22:35.650
That was a little embarrassing,
but I got to say how I feel.

00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:41.920
Sugisaki?

00:22:42.220 --> 00:22:43.220
Y-Yes?

00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:46.490
We want to say something to you, too.

00:22:47.230 --> 00:22:48.110
Key-kun.

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:49.060
Ken.

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:50.530
Senpai.

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:51.740
All together...

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:54.100
We love you, too!

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:58.510
The guy who said he
wanted a harem,

00:22:58.510 --> 00:23:01.100
even after we all glared at him.

00:23:01.100 --> 00:23:03.380
But who still sometimes helps us out.

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:04.610
Earnest.

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:05.820
Kind.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:09.120
But really such a dummy.

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:11.400
Everything about you...

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:13.320
We love you.

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:19.210
So please stay the skirt chaser
that you are now.

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:22.450
It's not like you to be
satisfied just by hearing

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:23.830
us say we like you.

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:27.870
Even without us,
stay just the way you are, okay?

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:29.470
Got it?

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:34.640
Yes.

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:40.200
I... I... I'm going
to be a harem master.

00:23:46.810 --> 00:23:48.080
A harem master!

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:49.710
Good luck!

00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:51.940
Listen to him!

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:54.230
I'm laughing so hard I can't breathe!

00:23:54.790 --> 00:23:56.270
You guys, that's mean!

00:24:04.990 --> 00:24:07.680
Let's all meet here after
the ceremony tomorrow.

00:24:08.860 --> 00:24:10.580
We're having a student
council meeting tomorrow?

00:24:10.580 --> 00:24:11.990
Of course.

00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:14.860
We're still the student
council until tomorrow ends.

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:15.690
Of course.

00:24:15.690 --> 00:24:16.320
Yeah.

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:18.450
Let's go, Sugisaki.

00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:20.530
Yeah!

00:24:21.090 --> 00:24:23.590
What should tomorrow's topic be?

00:24:23.590 --> 00:24:27.330
You need to focus on your
reply for the ceremony.

00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:29.980
I forgot!

00:24:29.980 --> 00:24:31.610
What do I do?

00:24:31.610 --> 00:24:32.720
Oh, President.

00:24:32.720 --> 00:24:34.290
You're not helping!

00:24:34.290 --> 00:24:35.340
Oh, President.
